1695 0 obj
<<
/Title (Why?  Balances detail vs. speed. Large enough to see facial features; small enough for fast training on CPU.  Learns 32 different low-level features \(edges, colours\) standard starting point.  Doubles capacity to learn more complex patterns in the deeper  layer.  With only 100 images, overfitting is a real risk. Dropout randomly  disables neurons during training, forcing the model to be robust.  Adaptive learning rate generally works well out-of-the-box without  manual tuning.  Ensures the two output values sum to 1.0, interpretable as  probabilities.)
/Dest [26 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1691 0 R
>>
endobj
